248
00:26:30.655 --> 00:26:32.020
And Shrek
took the ride with him.

249
00:26:32.123 --> 00:26:35.388
Shrek over here inside the car.
Well, Eddie, on behalf

250
00:26:35.527 --> 00:26:37.689
of Buzz Chew Chevrolet
and Cadillac,

251
00:26:37.796 --> 00:26:39.958
it was supposed to be their
night at the races last week.

252
00:26:40.098 --> 00:26:41.532
That's been rescheduled
for August 12th,

253
00:26:41.633 --> 00:26:44.329
but since you guys have
the nightoff, you get the, uh--

254
00:26:44.436 --> 00:26:46.097
the Buzz Chew trophy
here tonight.

255
00:26:46.237 --> 00:26:47.568
Congratulations.
A great run.

256
00:26:47.672 --> 00:26:49.436
- You're back.
- Thank you.

257
00:26:50.475 --> 00:26:52.534
- I can't even talk.
- It's got to be--

258
00:26:52.644 --> 00:26:54.408
No, let's talk about it.
It's been a hot day.

259
00:26:54.546 --> 00:26:56.640
How hot was it getting
inside this car?

260
00:26:57.115 --> 00:26:59.345
Very hot.
I'm, like, out of breath.

261
00:27:00.852 --> 00:27:03.822
This win was for my father.
Passed away...

262
00:27:04.289 --> 00:27:06.053
Yeah, and that was
dedicated to my dad.

263
00:27:07.158 --> 00:27:09.650
My dad died on
 the 29th of July,

264
00:27:10.328 --> 00:27:11.989
so this was
the win for my dad,

265
00:27:12.130 --> 00:27:14.224
so that's why I wanted
to show you the video.

266
00:27:15.567 --> 00:27:17.399
So it felt good to pull it off,

267
00:27:17.969 --> 00:27:20.597
and now we'll just keep winning
after that as much as we can.

268
00:27:21.573 --> 00:27:23.371
Next thing you know
I bought the car.

269
00:27:23.475 --> 00:27:25.000
I just bought
a new truck last week.

270
00:27:25.143 --> 00:27:27.202
Oh, yeah, I had just bought
a new truck too.

271
00:27:28.246 --> 00:27:30.146
So what'd you think
of the video, pretty good?

272
00:27:32.417 --> 00:27:34.112
We spoke about
when we met each other

273
00:27:34.252 --> 00:27:36.653
that you're gonna
back up on that.

274
00:27:37.622 --> 00:27:40.250
Now they are pushing you
to go back racing

275
00:27:40.959 --> 00:27:43.985
because you agreed that you
probably were not gonna do it.

276
00:27:44.295 --> 00:27:46.662
They are pushing you so much,
calling you so much,

277
00:27:46.798 --> 00:27:48.288
that you decided to do it,

278
00:27:49.501 --> 00:27:52.027
and you have to remember you
were planning to get married,

279
00:27:52.370 --> 00:27:53.804
having a house together.

280
00:27:53.905 --> 00:27:56.135
That's a lot of expenses
involved,

281
00:27:57.442 --> 00:27:59.638
-and all that.
- Well, I was hoping you're rich

282
00:27:59.744 --> 00:28:01.644
- so you could cover that.
- But I am not.

283
00:28:01.746 --> 00:28:03.771
I'm only kidding.

284
00:28:04.315 --> 00:28:06.409
- But I am not, and I--
- No, I understand that.

285
00:28:06.518 --> 00:28:08.179
I understand that.
Like you said.

286
00:28:08.687 --> 00:28:10.121
I guess it's in the blood.

287
00:28:10.221 --> 00:28:12.155
I followed
my father's footsteps.

288
00:28:12.891 --> 00:28:15.019
Been around the track
since I was born.

289
00:28:16.061 --> 00:28:16.994
Uh...

290
00:28:18.496 --> 00:28:20.328
Last time I saw my dad,

291
00:28:20.465 --> 00:28:22.365
I took a win for him
in New Jersey.

292
00:28:23.368 --> 00:28:25.427
I know my father had tears
in his eyes.

293
00:28:25.537 --> 00:28:28.063
He always says to me,
"You go do it,"

294
00:28:28.206 --> 00:28:30.470
he says,
"I know you'll be good at it."

295
00:28:30.575 --> 00:28:32.373
And when he saw
 me win, he goes,

296
00:28:32.510 --> 00:28:34.672
"Now I know you're gonna be
better than me,”

297
00:28:34.846 --> 00:28:36.814
he says,
"So don't ever give up on it."

298
00:28:37.382 --> 00:28:39.282
He says, "And if you love
what you're doing,

299
00:28:39.784 --> 00:28:42.048
don't stop till you
can't do it no more."”

300
00:28:42.854 --> 00:28:44.219
You have breathing problems.

301
00:28:44.355 --> 00:28:48.019
You having sinus problem.

302
00:28:48.126 --> 00:28:49.821
You have high cholesterol.

303
00:28:49.928 --> 00:28:52.363
You have all your heart
attacks and stents,

304
00:28:52.497 --> 00:28:54.363
and you have to...

305
00:28:55.667 --> 00:28:57.635
I think you forget
a little bit about that

306
00:28:57.736 --> 00:29:01.297
and worry about the racing
more than your health.

307
00:29:02.974 --> 00:29:05.875
Well, it's funny to say,
but when you get in a race car,

308
00:29:05.977 --> 00:29:07.536
you could have pain in your arm,

309
00:29:07.679 --> 00:29:09.010
soon as you get
on that racetrack,

310
00:29:09.114 --> 00:29:10.513
you don't have pain in your arm.

311
00:30:18.983 --> 00:30:20.542
Dalton, we can go this way.

312
00:30:37.635 --> 00:30:39.660
There's one in the front
and one in the back.

313
00:30:45.143 --> 00:30:46.440
They're German hornets.

314
00:30:46.678 --> 00:30:48.305
Do not slam
that ladder on there.

315
00:30:50.481 --> 00:30:52.609
It'll be one of the worst
mistakes you ever make.

316
00:30:53.318 --> 00:30:55.753
- Take this.
- You will get torn the fuck up.

317
00:32:08.226 --> 00:32:10.354
- What are you gonna have?
- Eggs.

318
00:32:11.296 --> 00:32:13.287
- Eggs?
- All-righty.

319
00:32:13.431 --> 00:32:15.593
- Bugsy, you make it. I'm--
- You guys set the table.

320
00:32:15.733 --> 00:32:16.894
I'll make the breakfast,
all right?

321
00:32:17.001 --> 00:32:18.662
You get the eggs
from down there already?

322
00:32:18.770 --> 00:32:20.067
Yeah,
I got 'em this morning.

323
00:32:20.171 --> 00:32:21.138
Yeah, okay.

324
00:32:21.272 --> 00:32:23.206
Somebody's got to wake
the chickens up.

325
00:32:23.942 --> 00:32:25.535
Had to wake
the goddamn chickens up,

326
00:32:25.643 --> 00:32:27.941
and sit around here for three
hours before you get here.

327
00:32:30.982 --> 00:32:34.145
Am I gonna need my, uh...
calm-me-down pills today or not?

328
00:32:34.319 --> 00:32:35.980
- What?
- I'll make a roll I guess.

329
00:32:36.120 --> 00:32:37.417
- Right?
- You don't want eggs?

330
00:32:37.555 --> 00:32:39.114
You can make me eggs,
but I'll eat a roll

331
00:32:39.257 --> 00:32:40.520
- in the meantime.
- All right.

332
00:32:40.658 --> 00:32:41.591
I see rolls there.

333
00:32:44.562 --> 00:32:46.394
I'm pretty sure--
Like, even last week.

334
00:32:47.165 --> 00:32:49.532
It cost you, what,
two wheels, two tires,

335
00:32:50.668 --> 00:32:51.965
and a week's worth of work.

336
00:32:53.171 --> 00:32:55.299
- Now--
- Rims, tie rod.

337
00:32:55.473 --> 00:32:59.068
New tie rod ends just from
his anger management problem.

338
00:33:02.547 --> 00:33:03.912
- But--
- Yeah, we need a win

339
00:33:04.048 --> 00:33:05.948
- to pay for it now.
- What goes around comes around.

340
00:33:06.050 --> 00:33:07.176
He bring it on himself.

341
00:35:12.510 --> 00:35:13.568
So now you got, like,

342
00:35:13.711 --> 00:35:15.543
- a few seconds now.
- Okay, ready?

343
00:35:15.646 --> 00:35:16.579
Al right.

344
00:35:17.281 --> 00:35:18.840
Just tell me about yourself.

345
00:35:18.950 --> 00:35:20.782
Tell me what you do
and where you're from

346
00:35:20.918 --> 00:35:23.888
- and what you do here.
- Well, I, um--

347
00:35:24.322 --> 00:35:25.448
Oh, okay, sure.

348
00:35:26.090 --> 00:35:27.888
Hi, everybody.
I just want to let you know

349
00:35:27.992 --> 00:35:31.929
that I been--
we been doing this filming here

350
00:35:32.063 --> 00:35:35.294
at Riverhead Raceway
for 25 years,

351
00:35:35.600 --> 00:35:37.261
and starting last week,

352
00:35:37.635 --> 00:35:39.501
we taped the whole show

353
00:35:40.004 --> 00:35:43.030
from start to finish here
at Riverhead Raceway,

354
00:35:43.307 --> 00:35:44.706
and then, um...

355
00:35:45.343 --> 00:35:48.040
I had fun
taking the tapes home at night,

356
00:35:48.146 --> 00:35:49.978
and replaying 'em,
and making copies

357
00:35:50.114 --> 00:35:53.607
for all the winners
out here at Riverhead Raceway.

358
00:35:56.988 --> 00:35:58.649
- Right, Bob?
- That's right.

359
00:36:03.327 --> 00:36:04.988
Oh, the-- Oh, the house?

360
00:36:05.129 --> 00:36:08.099
Alright , that came with
 the years of experience

361
00:36:08.199 --> 00:36:09.496
and my request.

362
00:36:09.934 --> 00:36:14.064
I-- We started down on
 the ground 25 years ago,

363
00:36:14.172 --> 00:36:16.072
and it was just
getting too crowded.

364
00:36:16.174 --> 00:36:18.108
People were walking in front
of the camera all the time,

365
00:36:18.209 --> 00:36:19.938
- so I moved up here for--
- Good evening,

366
00:36:20.111 --> 00:36:21.738
<i>ladies and gentlemen.
It's officially time...</i>

367
00:36:21.846 --> 00:36:23.507
So I'll see you later.
We're getting ready

368
00:36:23.648 --> 00:36:26.140
to go for the show.
So thanks a lot, everybody,

369
00:36:26.250 --> 00:36:28.480
and we'll talk to you later.
Thank you.

370
00:36:28.586 --> 00:36:29.747
Tonight, it--

371
00:37:39.123 --> 00:37:40.249
Whoa!

372
00:37:41.659 --> 00:37:42.751
Oh, God.

373
00:37:43.461 --> 00:37:45.429
- Oh!
- Is he out?

374
00:37:45.896 --> 00:37:46.761
No.

375
00:37:48.599 --> 00:37:49.725
Oh, God!

376
00:38:00.111 --> 00:38:01.579
Now, did you breathe in?

377
00:38:01.679 --> 00:38:03.078
Nope, I held my breath
the whole time.

378
00:38:03.214 --> 00:38:05.114
- The whole entire time?
- Yeah, that's ultimately

379
00:38:05.249 --> 00:38:06.580
what they told me
saved my life.

380
00:38:06.684 --> 00:38:08.379
/ mean, do you remember
it at all, besides--

381
00:38:08.486 --> 00:38:10.079
I remember it
from beginning to end.

382
00:38:10.254 --> 00:38:12.723
To the helicopter, to begging
the guy for more morphine,

383
00:38:12.823 --> 00:38:14.291
to almost wrecking
the helicopter.

384
00:38:14.425 --> 00:38:15.722
Going into the hospital.

385
00:38:15.926 --> 00:38:18.293
Getting put into an ice tank
to cool my body off.

386
00:38:18.696 --> 00:38:20.664
I remember the scrub downs.
I remember every shower.

387
00:38:20.798 --> 00:38:22.493
It was miserable.
That was the worst part.

388
00:38:22.900 --> 00:38:24.390
The ambulance wouldn't
come onto the track

389
00:38:24.502 --> 00:38:26.231
till the car fire went out.

390
00:38:26.337 --> 00:38:28.806
I had to sit there and wait
a good four or five minutes,

391
00:38:28.939 --> 00:38:30.600
and I was just talking
to my sister the whole time,

392
00:38:30.708 --> 00:38:33.040
<i>just trying to talk to her
'cause I looked down,</i>

393
00:38:33.144 --> 00:38:35.977
I saw my shinbone.
That's how bad my right leg was.

394
00:39:19.390 --> 00:39:21.154
Hit the window.
Hit the window.

395
00:39:22.293 --> 00:39:23.727
Come on,
you got to get the window.

396
00:39:24.595 --> 00:39:26.859
- That's the money shot.
- Is that it?

397
00:39:27.131 --> 00:39:28.565
That back window
is the money shot.

398
00:39:28.699 --> 00:39:29.996
My wrist is killing me.

399
00:39:30.134 --> 00:39:32.102
That back shots the w--
Oh, come on.

400
00:39:32.203 --> 00:39:33.830
- I'm not hitting the window.
- Come on.

401
00:39:33.971 --> 00:39:35.461
I got to clean up
the glass then, dude.

402
00:39:35.606 --> 00:39:37.370
- I'm not cleaning up glass.
- Ah, stop.

403
00:39:54.925 --> 00:39:56.154
Got bolts in there.

404
00:40:00.030 --> 00:40:00.861
Right there.

405
00:40:04.635 --> 00:40:05.602
Don't drop them bolts.

406
00:40:29.627 --> 00:40:31.254
This thing's heavier
and heavier.

407
00:40:31.495 --> 00:40:32.724
It never got lighter.

408
00:40:33.931 --> 00:40:36.263
- The heaviest car to push...
- Good.

409
00:40:36.434 --> 00:40:37.865
That's it.

410
00:40:40.371 --> 00:40:41.902
Flip it around.

411
00:40:45.109 --> 00:40:46.643
Is it on the wrong way?

412
00:40:47.244 --> 00:40:49.178
It's the wrong way, right?

413
00:40:50.581 --> 00:40:52.174
Just put it down.
There you go.

414
00:41:01.392 --> 00:41:03.383
- It's not flush.
- Just let go.

415
00:41:04.595 --> 00:41:06.029
I got to get this side first.

416
00:41:06.330 --> 00:41:08.492
- It's not good.
- It is good.

417
00:41:09.433 --> 00:41:11.128
The bolt right here
isn't lined up.

418
00:41:11.268 --> 00:41:12.667
It will line up.

419
00:41:15.072 --> 00:41:16.130
Right here.

420
00:41:18.509 --> 00:41:19.635
This one, Dad.

421
00:41:59.917 --> 00:42:01.783
Seventeen-year-old

422
00:42:01.919 --> 00:42:04.354
Jack Handley Jr. out of Medford

423
00:42:05.856 --> 00:42:07.722
Last week he won the race,

424
00:42:08.592 --> 00:42:12.426
but post-race tech was found
with an unapproved cam shaft.

425
00:42:12.530 --> 00:42:14.191
Oversized.

426
00:42:14.565 --> 00:42:16.190
The team, Dennis Krupski

427
00:42:16.200 --> 00:42:19.795
and the Liccardi Builders
49 team went to work.

428
00:42:20.070 --> 00:42:22.038
Lots of hours in the shop.

429
00:42:22.172 --> 00:42:25.574
Another motor,
another cam shaft in the car,

430
00:42:25.709 --> 00:42:27.905
and it did not matter.

431
00:42:28.045 --> 00:42:32.039
Jack Handley Jr.
is a winner here tonight

432
00:42:32.182 --> 00:42:34.742
at Riverhead Raceway,
and if there was ever a way

433
00:42:34.885 --> 00:42:37.479
to atone for the DQ last week,

434
00:42:37.588 --> 00:42:40.182
this young Patchogue-Medford
High School student

435
00:42:40.324 --> 00:42:41.917
showed you how it's done.

436
00:42:52.102 --> 00:42:54.230
That's my son's trunk lid.

437
00:42:55.606 --> 00:42:58.041
You know, he bought this car
and started driving it around,

438
00:42:58.175 --> 00:43:00.234
and I says, "You know,
that's just like my race car.”

439
00:43:00.377 --> 00:43:03.074
I says, "I'm gonna get
that car one day for parts.”

440
00:43:03.514 --> 00:43:04.572
He said, "No way."

441
00:43:05.549 --> 00:43:07.847
Well, he ended up
blowing the motor in the car,

442
00:43:08.552 --> 00:43:10.213
bought a new one,
and here it is.

443
00:43:10.554 --> 00:43:13.148
I got his whole car back here.

444
00:43:13.591 --> 00:43:15.184
Doors, fenders, hoods.

445
00:43:15.292 --> 00:43:17.026
I can't carry them all out,

446
00:43:17.227 --> 00:43:19.753
but there's a story
behind each piece.

447
00:43:19.897 --> 00:43:21.490
These are all my spare parts.

448
00:43:21.599 --> 00:43:23.567
For anybody that wants
to get rough with me,

449
00:43:23.667 --> 00:43:26.398
go for it because I got--
I got it covered.

450
00:43:27.137 --> 00:43:29.731
That's why I'm not afraid to hit
none of you guys out there.

451
00:43:30.007 --> 00:43:32.032
That's why you're all mad
at me all the time.

452
00:43:32.142 --> 00:43:34.543
But anyway, on my spare time

453
00:43:34.645 --> 00:43:36.272
when I'm not working
on my race car,

454
00:43:37.114 --> 00:43:41.051
I actually have
a soft side of me

455
00:43:41.151 --> 00:43:42.346
that likes to garden.

456
00:43:42.987 --> 00:43:45.081
He-- Right here
we got my tomato plants,

457
00:43:45.489 --> 00:43:47.924
which are always the best.
I make tomato sauce.

458
00:43:48.626 --> 00:43:51.118
The best.
And then I have my flowers.

459
00:43:51.261 --> 00:43:53.793
The reason for the flowers and
the tomatoes next to each other

460
00:43:53.931 --> 00:43:56.593
is 'cause the bumble bees
like the flowers,

461
00:43:57.134 --> 00:43:58.898
and they pollinate the tomatoes,

462
00:43:59.570 --> 00:44:01.299
if anybody knows
anything about that.

463
00:44:02.039 --> 00:44:03.234
I have blueberries.

464
00:44:04.475 --> 00:44:06.534
Blueberries every spring.
Beautiful.

465
00:44:06.644 --> 00:44:09.079
No problem.
My morning glories.

466
00:44:09.179 --> 00:44:11.509
You come out here in the morning,
this whole bush is lit up.

467
00:44:12.950 --> 00:44:15.419
And we end up over here

468
00:44:16.320 --> 00:44:18.948
by the raspberries that you
could see are full of bees.

469
00:44:19.056 --> 00:44:20.990
That's why they're here too
'cause the raspberries .

470
00:44:21.125 --> 00:44:24.459
Actually, the bees love
the raspberry smell,

471
00:44:25.663 --> 00:44:27.453
and the bees pollinate
everything else.

472
00:44:27.464 --> 00:44:28.990
You have to have bees.

473
00:44:29.033 --> 00:44:31.033
You don't have any bees,
you don't have any garden.

474
00:44:31.035 --> 00:44:33.129
Plain and simple.
It's the way it works.

475
00:44:43.447 --> 00:44:45.108
All right, can you--
You can hear me?

476
00:44:45.916 --> 00:44:46.974
Okay, great.

477
00:44:47.151 --> 00:44:48.243
It's, uh--

478
00:44:48.385 --> 00:44:52.253
I'm standing across the street
from the Riverhead Raceway,

479
00:44:53.057 --> 00:44:56.186
right in front of Route 58,
which is now a four-lane road

480
00:44:56.660 --> 00:45:00.688
with about 26,000 cars
going by a day.

481
00:45:01.065 --> 00:45:03.159
The property
that I'm standing on right now

482
00:45:03.300 --> 00:45:05.667
used to be all woods,
about 40 acres,

483
00:45:05.769 --> 00:45:08.329
and it was cleared
in a matter of days.

484
00:45:08.472 --> 00:45:11.339
Uh, it's the future home
of a large shopping center

485
00:45:11.475 --> 00:45:13.307
with Costco and about--

486
00:45:13.410 --> 00:45:16.641
The first phase is about
270,000 square feet,

487
00:45:16.747 --> 00:45:20.650
and the next phase is probably
another 200,000 square feet.

488
00:45:20.751 --> 00:45:24.085
So this is really ground zero
for development

489
00:45:24.221 --> 00:45:25.916
around the Riverhead Raceway.

490
00:45:26.056 --> 00:45:27.182
Across the street,

491
00:45:28.025 --> 00:45:29.652
you have a 13-acre
piece of property

492
00:45:29.760 --> 00:45:31.228
that used to be all wooded.

493
00:45:31.361 --> 00:45:33.489
That was cleared
in a matter of days.

